==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|twai|lang=gem-pro}}, whence also Old English {{term|twa|twā|lang=ang}} (English {{term|two|lang=en}}), Old Frisian {{term|twa|twā|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|twa#Old Saxon|twā}}, {{term|two#Old Saxon|twō}}, Dutch {{term|twee|lang=nl}}, German {{term|zwei|lang=de}}, Gothic {{term|𐍄𐍅𐌰𐌹|tr=twai|lang=got}}. Compare also Old English {{term|twegen|twēġen|lang=ang}} (English {{term|twain|lang=en}}), Old Saxon {{term|twene|twēne|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|zwene|zwēne|lang=goh}} (German {{term|zween|lang=de}}). Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|dwó|lang=ine-pro}}, whence also Latin {{term|duo|lang=la}}, Ancient Greek {{term|δύο|tr=dúo|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Numeral===
{{head|non|numeral}}

# {{cardinal|lang=non}} [[two]]

